articles.content_en:
Article 1 An Internet Court shall have centralized jurisdiction over the following first-instance cases that shall be accepted by a Primary People's Court within the municipality where the Internet Court is located:
(1) disputes over ownership, infringement, and contracts relating to network data;
(2) disputes over protection of personal information and right to privacy on the network;
(3) disputes over ownership, infringement, and contracts relating to virtual property on the network;
(4) disputes over unfair competition on the network;
(5) disputes over ownership, infringement, and contracts relating to domain names on the network;
(6) disputes arising from the conclusion or performance of online shopping contracts through e-commerce platforms;
(7) disputes over network service contracts the conclusion and performance of which are both completed on the network;
(8) administrative disputes arising from administrative acts such as network data supervision, supervision of personal information protection on the network, supervision of unfair competition on the network, network transaction management, and network information service management by administrative organs; and
(9) network public interest lawsuits initiated by the procuratorial organs.
Foreign-related civil cases that meet the provisions of the preceding paragraph, as well as civil cases involving the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, the Macao Special Administrative Region, and the Taiwan region, shall be under the jurisdiction of the Internet Court.
With the approval of the Supreme People's Court, the relevant Higher People's Court may designate the Internet Court to have jurisdiction over other specific types of network-related civil and administrative cases.
